# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output — never committed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
build
.build
.swiftpm
Derived/
*.xcresult

# Compiled Python bytecode. Written next to the research scripts whenever one of them is imported,
# and tagged with the local interpreter version, so it is machine-specific by construction.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated Xcode projects — NEVER tracked.
#
# A generated project is not source. The source of truth is the XcodeGen spec that sits next to it:
#
#   Examples/ScreenGuardDemo/project.yml   -> Examples/ScreenGuardDemo/ScreenGuardDemo.xcodeproj
#   Research/CaptureMatrix/project.yml     -> Research/CaptureMatrix/CaptureMatrix.xcodeproj
#
# `mise run generate` rebuilds both from those specs with the mise-pinned XcodeGen, and
# `Scripts/verify_capture.sh` — the documented one-command verification — regenerates the demo
# project from project.yml automatically when it is missing, so a fresh clone needs neither a
# committed project nor a separate XcodeGen install. Committing the bundle would only let it drift
# away from the spec it was generated from.
#
# There is deliberately no `!Examples/**/*.xcodeproj`-style negation: every .xcodeproj and
# .xcworkspace in this tree is generated, including `<project>.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace`,
# which is part of the bundle and is regenerated with it. The shared scheme that
# `xcodebuild -scheme ScreenGuardDemo` requires is declared under `scheme:` in
# Examples/ScreenGuardDemo/project.yml and is generated with the project.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.xcodeproj
*.xcworkspace

# Per-user Xcode state, written whenever a project is opened or built. Machine-specific, churns
# constantly, and means nothing to anyone else. It lives inside the generated bundle, so these
# rules only matter for a bundle that is already on disk.
xcuserdata/
*.xcuserstate
*.xcuserdatad

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AgentTeams runtime state.
#
# Task graph, mailboxes, attempt ids and progress for the team session that built this repository.
# Tool-managed, machine- and session-specific, and rewritten continuously while a team runs — so
# committing it would produce churn and conflicts with no product value. Everything it produced
# that matters was distilled into `docs/evidence/` and the amendment ledger in
# `docs/api-contract.md` §13, so no finding lives only here.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
.agent-teams/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Measurement artifacts.
#
# Raw output of the capture-matrix harness (PNGs, logs, JSON) — regenerable with
# `Research/Scripts/capture_matrix.sh`. Only the canonical runs cited by
# `docs/evidence/capability-matrix.md` §1 are committed, so every number in that document has its
# raw evidence in the repository, without carrying every experiment ever run (12 MB -> ~3.3 MB).
#
# The parent directory must stay trackable for the negations to work: git cannot re-include a file
# whose parent directory is excluded.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Research/Artifacts/*
!Research/Artifacts/20261002-151754-matrix/
!Research/Artifacts/20261002-151341-feasibility/
!Research/Artifacts/20261002-151448-replayKit/
!Research/Artifacts/20261002-153117-renderSanity/
